  "notes": "El Chocón’s curved rockfill crest, four radial gates and six-unit powerhouse follow the retained Limay site. The sloped dry outfall runs from the chutes to the mapped river. The reservoir intake retains its separate footbridge. The 386 m crest road meets the rendered approaches within 5 cm at both sampled centerlines. The east approach clears the fitted concrete supports. The two parts of the mapped water relation use representative stages of 370.65 m upstream and 315.43 m downstream. The access deck stays below the powerhouse windows. The water stages and spillway cross-sections are representative estimates. The outfall banks are faceted to follow the available terrain. A steep shore remains visible beyond the fitted works. The model shows the gates closed and the spillway dry. Plant interiors and operating flow are outside this exterior scope.",
